#X obj 60 1660 s \$0-vrs23;
#X text 82 1696 Choose slot 0-15: the current slot is stored  \, the new one \; loaded. An empty slot takes the current sound. \; The values are kept in [text define -k vrs23-kit] and saved \; with this patch. The same logic as in skandrums: \; outlet 2 -> skpreset left  \, skpreset left -> vrs23~ right., f 64;
#X obj 60 1816 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Inlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1840 0: audio (mono) \; 1: messages (see Messages below), f 64;
#X obj 60 1918 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Outlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1942 0: audio left  \, 1: audio right \; 2: events: dump  \, value, f 64;
#X obj 60 2020 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Messages 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2044 <control> <0-127>: set a control by name  \, e.g. regn 64 \; ctl <index> <value>  \, params v0 v1 ...: set by index \; defaults  \, reset: all controls to their defaults \; get <control>: answers 'value <control> <v>' on outlet 2 \; print: controls and sample rate to the Pd window \; dump: all controls on outlet 2 as 'dump vrs23 v0 ..' \; dump vrs23 v0 v1 ...: restore such a dump, f 64;
#X obj 60 2217 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Controls\ (index\ name\ default) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2241 0 inp (64) Input Volume: input level -24...+24 dB (64 = 0 \;    dB) \; 1 regn (0) Regeneration: feedback (dual pot \, -log) \; 2 key (3) [0-3] Delay key: 0 = 50  \, 1 = 100  \, 2 = 200  \, 3 = \;    400 ms (Reverb: E F G H) \; 3 mode (0) [0-1] Mode: 0 = echo  \, 1 = reverb \; 4 fine (0) Delay fine: 0 = longest time  \, 127 = shortest. \;    Changes the clock: what is in the buffer goes \;    higher/lower as in the original \; 5 swp (40) Sweep Freq: LFO 0.1...10 Hz \; 6 dpth (0) Depth: LFO depth on the clock \; 7 tone (64) Tone: 0 = dark  \, 127 = open \; 8 rtrn (100) Return: effect level L and R \; 9 fx (1) [0-1] Foot switch: 1 = effect on  \, 0 = input to the \;    effect muted (the tail rings out) \; 10 mix (64) Mix: 0 = dry only  \, 127 = effect only \; 11 vol (100) Output level: 100 = 0 dB  \, 0 = muted \; 12 cmpd (1) [0-1] Compander NE570 on (1) or off (0) \; 13 ctau (55) Compander time constant 0.5...100 ms (55 = \;    about 5 ms) \; 14 trck (64) Expander tracking error: +-3 dB (64 = 0) \; 15 nois (50) BBD noise: -100...-36 dB below nominal level \; 16 drv (64) BBD saturation: drive (64 = clipping from about \;    +10 dB) \; 17 aafc (64) Anti-aliasing filter: cutoff x0.5...x2 \; 18 aaq (0) Anti-aliasing filter: 0 = Butterworth  \, 127 = as \;    read from the schematic \; 19 rkfc (64) Reconstruction filter: cutoff x0.5...x2 \; 20 rkq (0) Reconstruction filter: 0 = Butterworth  \, 127 = as \;    read from the schematic \; 21 emph (127) Pre-/de-emphasis: 0 = off  \, 127 = as in the \;    schematic \; 22 clka (0) Clock artefacts: sample-and-hold at f_clk \;    (aliasing) \; 23 rclk (0) [0-1] Clock of the upper row in reverb: 0 = 19 \;    kHz  \, 1 = 30.75 kHz \; 24 rnge (64) Range of delay fine: clock factor max. 1...4 \;    (64 = 2.5) \; 25 lfom (64) LFO swing at depth 127: 0...+-30 % of the clock \; 26 gmax (100) Maximum regeneration in echo (100 = just below \;    self-oscillation) \; 27 rvgm (70) Maximum regeneration in reverb (70 = tail of \;    about 5 s at full turn  \, self-oscillation from about 90) \; 28 fxlv (64) Effect level trim: +-12 dB \; 29 bias (78) BBD bias (P17/P18): 64 = symmetric  \, 78 = \;    slightly asymmetric  \, else even harmonics (H2) \; 30 iclp (58) Input stage I001: clipping headroom 0...24 dB \;    above nominal level (58 = about 11 dB) \; 31 cclp (54) Compressor output (P11): soft limit 0...24 dB \;    above nominal level, f 64;
#X obj 60 3231 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Signal\ path 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 3255 input -> pre-emphasis -> E1/E2 -> NE570 compressor -> \; anti-aliasing -> 2 x 5 BBD chips (768 clocks each) -> taps -> \; reconstruction -> NE570 expander -> A1/A2 -> tone  \, return. \; Echo: 10 chips in series  \, one clock  \, mono output. \; Reverb: rows separate  \, two clocks  \, cross-coupled. \; L = lower row  \, R = upper row. \; The buffer follows the clock: fine and sweep change the \; pitch of what is already in the bucket brigade., f 64;
#X obj 60 3447 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Credits 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 3471 Credits: Modelled on the Dynacord schematics 80 207 / 80 205 \; (1981) and the service manual (1983) with help by Claude. \; skpreset from skandrums-pd (CC0). Reference: vrs23-clap.wav, f 64;
